    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change was to the create audit line emitted by `AuditOwnerCreated` (the `POST /api/owners` audit step), which now also logs `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel` alongside the fields it already logged.\n\n`membershipLevel` was already present, so the substantive addition was `membershipNumber`. Rather than copy the `<customerCode>-M<YY>` derivation, I reused the existing `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber(Owner)` \u2014 the single source of truth for that format \u2014 by injecting `OwnerMapper` into the step (the mapper is already an injectable bean, used the same way by `RespondWithOwnerCreated` and other steps):\n\n```java\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper) {\n    AUDIT.info(\"Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipPoints={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n            owner.getMembershipPoints(), owner.getMembershipLevel(),\n            ownerMapper.membershipNumber(owner));\n}\n```\n\nThe javadoc was updated to match, and all previously-logged fields remain. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes and no existing tests regressed.",
